  "slug": "phases-symtft-1132",
  "summary": "Five preprints in mid-November 2026 extend symmetry-based classification, from the SymTFT and subsystem SPT response theory to higher-order and half-chiral phases.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is how symmetry structure constrains and classifies gapped and topological phases. A review presents the SymTFT framework for generalized symmetries, anomalies, and phase classification. A lattice response theory for subsystem SPT phases links response actions to cluster entanglers. Three further works concern lattice topology under unconventional symmetry: an intrinsic chiral higher-order topological phase stabilized by a single diagonal reflection in a quarter-plane, phases protected by half-chiral symmetry acting on one sublattice with real-space invariants, and a generalized spectral localizer giving Z and Z2 invariants for hinge, Dirac-node, and valley modes. What is new is the extension of protecting symmetries and of invariants, rather than a single shared method.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
